{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L89","fileName":"NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","text":"ArraySlice"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successors.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The components are those of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":" without the trivial ones, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Empty exactly when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attractingComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":", so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices do not start at 0."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":", so one sort by that vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position puts the components in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", where positions are insertion order:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Vertex","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","te